So... I've combined the weird `RestorableKeyBindingRow` class with the old one. To make this work, I had to add one workaround to the `RestoreDefaultsButton`, which is to have it handling focus. If this isn't done, the focus request will propagate upwards and be handled by the `KeyBindingRow` (this is framework behaviour).

@smoogipoo please review this one for me and make sure you're okay with the above.

I did dabble with moving all the focus to the `KeyButton` itself, which seems like the more appropriate place to handle it, but it complicates the event flow when the user clicks between buttons in the same row. Might be something we consider in  the future if refactoring this component further, but I'm just looking to keep changes to a minimum for now (which is why I combined the classes in the first place).
